WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
Another performance enhancement we can have on a network is to control the way resources are used as it pertains to the traffic they take up on a network.

00:09.000 --> 00:22.758
This is done through QoS, Quality of Service. To demonstrate QoS, I am in the QoS setup area of this wireless router. I'm going to set up a QoS rule, as we've enabled QoS.

00:22.758 --> 00:27.017
And for this example, this particular company uses Skype quite a bit,

00:27.017 --> 00:37.496
so I am going to give Skype traffic the highest priority here, through clicking the drop-down arrow on Service Names and looking for Skype.

00:37.496 --> 00:57.431
Then I'll click Add, and I'll give this a priority of Maximum, and then I will save these changes.

00:57.431 --> 01:05.675
So now, using Quality of Service, Skype traffic has Maximum priority on this network.

01:05.675 --> 01:11.388
Overall, Quality of Service focuses on five specific problems with data transfers:

01:11.388 --> 01:25.122
delay, dropped packets, errors, jitter, which is an inconsistency in signals, and out-of-order delivery. Giving a service higher priority will help negate those problems.

